@page "/diff"

@*
    Standalone paste-two-texts diff tool, on the design system's archetype 11
    (.pw frame + .cmp compare body - see .design/handoff/PageCompare.dc.html).
    The same frame as the Object Explorer's file diff, because it is the same
    screen with a different source for the two sides.

    Displayed as "Diff" since #578: "compare" is reserved for the Object
    Explorer's release/object/file comparison, and this audience owns "diff".
    The route is /diff; /compare still resolves, via CompareLegacyRedirect.razor.

    The two side-by-side panes ARE the input: they're editable CodeMirror
    editors (mountCompareEditor). As you type or paste, source-viewer.js
    debounces and POSTs both texts to /api/compare/diff, which reuses the same
    DiffPlex + SideBySideDiffSerializer pipeline the Object Explorer compare
    page renders, then swaps the diff decorations into both panes in place
    (setDiff) - no remount, so typed text and undo history survive.

    Static SSR, no [Authorize] and no Blazor circuit: like the Object Explorer
    viewer, all interactivity lives in source-viewer.js. Works without an
    account; nothing is stored server-side. The page is just the shell -
    source-viewer.js owns the editors, the live re-diff, the summary read-out,
    and the Swap / Clear / change-navigation controls (wired by their
    data-* attributes below). Those attributes and /api/compare/diff keep the
    "compare" spelling: they are shared with the Object Explorer's diff views,
    where the word is still the right one.
*@

<PageTitle>Diff · AL Dev Toolbox</PageTitle>

<div class="pw u-compact">
    <div class="pw__head">
        <div class="pw__title">
            <h1 class="pw__name">Diff</h1>
            <span class="pw__file">Paste two versions of any text to see what changed</span>
        </div>

        <span class="pw__spacer"></span>

        @* Both start switched off: there is nothing to swap or clear on an
           empty page, and a live button that does nothing is a worse first
           impression than one that waits its turn. source-viewer.js enables
           them as soon as either side has text. *@
        <button type="button" class="btn btn--sm" data-compare-swap disabled>
            <Icon Name="arrow-left-right" Width="14" Height="14" Css="btn__icon" />
            <span>Swap sides</span>
        </button>
        <button type="button" class="btn btn--sm" data-compare-clear disabled>
            <Icon Name="trash-2" Width="14" Height="14" Css="btn__icon" />
            <span>Clear both</span>
        </button>
    </div>

    <div class="pw__bar">
        <div class="vsbar">
            <span class="vs">
                <span class="vs__side">
                    <span class="vs__label">Left</span>
                    <span class="vs__name">The original</span>
                </span>
                <Icon Name="arrow-right" Css="vs__arrow" />
                <span class="vs__side">
                    <span class="vs__label">Right</span>
                    <span class="vs__name">The changed version</span>
                </span>
            </span>
        </div>

        <span class="pw__sep"></span>
        @* Where the file diff puts the same control. Hidden until both sides
           have text: before that there is no result to lay out, and the first
           thing to do on this page is get text in - offering a choice of how to
           render nothing is a choice about the wrong thing. source-viewer.js
           reveals it on the first diff and hides it again on Clear both. *@
        <span class="pill-tabs" role="group" aria-label="Diff layout" data-diff-layout hidden>
            <button class="pill-tab is-active" type="button" data-layout="side">Side by side</button>
            <button class="pill-tab" type="button" data-layout="inline">Inline</button>
        </span>

        @* A real checkbox here, where the Object Explorer's copy of this
           control is a link: that page has no circuit and puts its state in
           the URL, while this one already re-diffs from JS on every keystroke
           and has no URL to put anything in. Same label, same default. *@
        <label class="check">
            <input type="checkbox" data-compare-ignore-ws checked />
            <span class="check__box"><Icon Name="check" Width="12" Height="12" /></span>Ignore whitespace
        </label>

        <span class="pw__spacer"></span>
    </div>

    <div class="pw__body">
        @* No change rail: the two panes are the whole comparison, so there is
           no list of other files to walk. *@
        @* The server's per-side cap, published so source-viewer.js can say
           "too large" without first uploading the text that is too large. The
           number comes from the endpoint itself so the two can't drift. *@
        <div class="cmp cmp--norail" data-compare-max-length="@ALDevToolbox.Endpoints.CompareEndpoints.MaxInputLength">
            <div class="cmp__view">
                <div class="cmp__vbar">
                    @* The live read-out. Sits where the file diff puts its
                       "+14 -6", because it answers the same question. *@
                    @* Matches the string source-viewer.js writes back after
                       Clear both, so the same state never has two labels. The
                       instruction itself is in the head, where it stays put. *@
                    <span class="cmp__vname" data-compare-summary>Nothing to compare yet.</span>
                    <span class="pw__spacer"></span>
                    <span class="kbd-hint">
                        <span class="kbd" data-mod-key>Ctrl</span><span class="kbd">Down</span><span class="kbd-hint__label">next change</span>
                    </span>
                    <button type="button" class="btn btn--icon btn--sm" data-diff-nav="prev" disabled
                            aria-label="Previous change" title="Jump to the previous change (Ctrl + Up arrow)">
                        <Icon Name="chevron-up" Width="14" Height="14" Css="btn__icon" />
                    </button>
                    <button type="button" class="btn btn--icon btn--sm" data-diff-nav="next" disabled
                            aria-label="Next change" title="Jump to the next change (Ctrl + Down arrow)">
                        <Icon Name="chevron-down" Width="14" Height="14" Css="btn__icon" />
                    </button>
                </div>

                <div class="cmp__panes" data-layout-pane="side">
                    <div class="cmp__pane cmp__pane--host" role="group" aria-label="Original text">
                        <div class="cmp__phead">
                            <span class="refchip refchip--base">Original</span>
                        </div>
                        <div class="source-viewer source-viewer--compare" data-pane="left">
                            <div class="source-viewer__code"
                                 data-language="text"
                                 data-editable="true"
                                 data-content=""
                                 data-placeholder="Paste the original version here"
                                 spellcheck="false"></div>
                        </div>
                    </div>
                    <div class="cmp__pane cmp__pane--host" role="group" aria-label="Changed text">
                        <div class="cmp__phead">
                            <span class="refchip refchip--target">Changed</span>
                        </div>
                        <div class="source-viewer source-viewer--compare" data-pane="right">
                            <div class="source-viewer__code"
                                 data-language="text"
                                 data-editable="true"
                                 data-content=""
                                 data-placeholder="Paste the changed version here"
                                 spellcheck="false"></div>
                        </div>
                    </div>
                </div>

                @* The inline layout. A RESULT view, not a third input: one
                   read-only pane over a document the server synthesises from
                   both sides, rebuilt on every re-diff. Editing happens in
                   Side by side, which is why the head says so rather than
                   leaving someone to discover it by typing into a pane that
                   will not take a keystroke.

                   Starts empty and hidden. CodeMirror measures nothing useful
                   inside a hidden container, so source-viewer.js mounts this
                   the first time the reader switches to it - and remounts it
                   whenever the text behind it has moved on. *@
                <div class="cmp__panes cmp__panes--inline" data-layout-pane="inline" hidden>
                    <div class="cmp__pane cmp__pane--host" role="group" aria-label="Inline diff">
                        <div class="cmp__phead">
                            <span class="refchip refchip--base">Original</span>
                            <Icon Name="arrow-right" Css="vs__arrow" />
                            <span class="refchip refchip--target">Changed</span>
                            <span class="pw__spacer"></span>
                            <span class="u-muted">Read-only — switch to Side by side to edit</span>
                        </div>
                        <div class="source-viewer source-viewer--compare source-viewer--inline" data-pane="inline">
                            <div class="source-viewer__code"
                                 data-language="text"
                                 data-content=""
                                 spellcheck="false"></div>
                        </div>
                    </div>
                </div>
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>

    <div class="pw__foot">
        <span>Your text is sent to this server to compare it, and never stored</span>
        <span class="pw__sep"></span>
        <span class="kbd-hint">
            <span class="kbd" data-mod-key>Ctrl</span><span class="kbd">Down</span><span class="kbd-hint__label">next change</span>
        </span>
        <span class="kbd-hint">
            <span class="kbd" data-mod-key>Ctrl</span><span class="kbd">Up</span><span class="kbd-hint__label">previous</span>
        </span>
        <span data-layout-only="side">Scrolling either side moves the other</span>
        <span data-layout-only="inline" hidden>Old text above new; click a band to show the unchanged code</span>
    </div>
</div>
